WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.400
When it comes to something
as life-and-death important

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.120
as what to feed ourselves
and our families,

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.760
we should rely not on
anecdotes, but on facts.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.320
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.160
Have you ever heard of the
trendelenburg position?

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.160
Lying in this position at
a slight head down tilt

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.800
may actually help
you burn fat.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.920
Here’s the first story.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.000
When our blood volume drops,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.280
our kidneys detect it
and angiotensin is released.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.320
When our blood volume rises,
on the other hand,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.680
our heart detects it and
releases a hormone called ANP

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.840
(atrial natriuretic peptide,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.920
also known as ANF,
atrial natriuretic factor).

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.520
We used to think our heart
was just a pump,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.040
but now we know
it's also a gland.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.840
There are stretch receptors in
the first chamber of our heart,

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:56.840
and when extra blood pours into
the heart, ANP is released.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.040
What does it do?

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.840
As the title of a review
in an obesity journal put it:

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.600
"Heart hormones
fueling a fire in fat."

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.480
If you drip ANP on human fat
and muscle tissue,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.960
fat is rapidly released

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.280
and the muscle cells ramp up
their capacity to burn it.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.960
Infuse ANP into people

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.480
and the rate at which fat
is mobilized and burned

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:19.600
can shoot up 15 percent.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.760
You can take muscle biopsies
from people and show

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.080
how much better their muscles
get at burning fat

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.240
in the presence
of elevated ANP levels.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.320
No surprise then,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.040
that obese
and overweight individuals

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.080
tend to have
considerably lower levels

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.560
in their bloodstream.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.400
So, the way
to a person's stomach

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.640
may be through their heart.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:41.160
Why would this
stretch-sensitive heart hormone

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.920
tap into our fat stores?

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.520
Well, when does the heart
get stretched?

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.480
During intense
physical activity.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.240
We used to think it was just
the adrenaline-type hormones

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.040
that are released
when you exercise

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.840
that mobilized fat
from our tissues,

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.800
but now we know
that ANP from our heart

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.880
plays a key role as well.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.520
Inject people
with the amount of ANP

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.200
they'd normally get
in their system when exercising,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.440
and their whole-body fat burning
goes up,

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.120
even if they're just sitting
on the couch.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.080
How else
can we stretch our heart

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.480
that extra little bit
to release ANP?

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.160
By increasing our blood volume
by drinking extra water.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.400
When you don't drink
for 12 hours straight,

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.160
your ANP levels in your blood
fall by about 25 percent,

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.320
but chug down
about four glasses of water

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:28.240
and your levels
can jump up by 50 percent

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.680
within 90 minutes.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.720
Now that's too much
to drink at one time,

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.200
but it can offer a sense

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.600
of how much potential control
we have

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.240
over this fat-burning hormone.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.520
How else
could we trick our body

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.560
into producing
this exercise hormone

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.040
without lacing up
our gym shoes?

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.720
If it's all about pooling
extra blood into our heart,

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.200
what about lying
with our head tilted down?

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.480
It sounds kind of funny,

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.960
but researchers took
the possibility seriously enough

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.880
to run the experiment.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.760
They laid people down
at just a six-degree angle,

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.080
a slight tilt that's like
putting three or four bricks

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.800
under the posts
at the foot of your bed.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.240
So, it's not like
you're hanging upside down.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.920
They were almost flat
but at just enough of a slant

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.800
for gravity to draw extra blood
into their torso.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.000
Within an hour,
their ANP levels doubled

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.720
and stayed up for the four hours
the experiment ran.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.280
Okay, but did they
all of a sudden

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.760
start burning more fat?

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.760
Yes, the proportion of fat
they were burning as fuel

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.320
shot up by 40 percent,

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.880
and they were just lying down
the whole time.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:36.760
So, what if you tried sleeping
with a slight head-down tilt

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.400
by putting a few bricks
under the posts

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.240
at the foot of your bed?

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.680
Would it cause you to burn
more fat while you slept?

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:49.200
I'll address the potential pros
and cons next.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.440
I noted how lying
at a slight, six-degree,

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:58.720
head-down tilt for a few hours
can boost fat burning.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.200
Now obviously you wouldn't want
to lie tilted back

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.360
if you had a heart condition,

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.440
such as
congestive heart failure.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.640
As many as 8 to 12 cups
(1.90 to 2.90 L) of blood

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.760
may be displaced into the torso
from the extremities

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.440
at a tilt like that,

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.320
so you have to have
the cardiovascular fitness

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.920
to handle it.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.800
Acid reflux
could also be a problem.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.920
In fact, we typically tell
heartburn patients

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.280
to do the reverse,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.800
put a few bricks
under the posts

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.000
at the head of their bed

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.040
to have gravity work
in their favor

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.000
to keep stomach acid
down where it belongs.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.240
But for those
without medical problems,

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:34.600
is there a harm to lying
tilted back for a few hours?

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:38.280
Well, it could give you
a "space headache."

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:41.680
In movies, astronauts are shown
practicing underwater,

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.000
but the gold standard
for simulating

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.280
the physiological effects
of the weightlessness

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:51.600
of outer space is HDBR,
head-down bed rest.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.040
On Earth, our blood tends
to collect in our legs,

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.400
so our body is designed
to force blood headward.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.680
In outer space,
our body is still trying

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.080
to push our blood "up,"

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.040
so without Earth's gravity,

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.080
blood pushes upwards
to our head and chest,

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.320
just like it does
when we lie tilted back.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:13.720
This realization
came from cosmonauts

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:15.720
returning from
the space station

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.240
feeling as though
they were slipping

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.640
towards the foot of the bed,

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.480
and only feeling "normal"

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.680
when they were tilted
six degrees back.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.480
All of the extra blood
pooling in the head

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.240
is thought to contribute
to the headaches

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.000
reported by up to 70 percent
of astronauts

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.240
during space flights,

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.760
and a similar percentage
of individuals suffer headaches

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.000
from prolonged
head-down bed rest.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.960
That's after days, though.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.120
In preparation
for a mission to Mars,

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.960
space agencies put people
through head-down bed rest

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.680
for prolonged periods,

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.080
eating, bathing,
and toileting

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.800
all while lying in bed

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:53.120
tilted back
for literally months at a time.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.840
Extended stretches
of head-down positioning

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:58.120
for weeks may impair
lung function,

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.320
brain function,
and immune function,

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.480
and cause a loss
of muscle mass.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.280
On the last Apollo mission,

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.400
the astronauts lost
about five pounds (2.30 kg)

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.320
of fat over the 12-day trip,

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.880
but they also lost
about two pounds (0.90 kg)

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.640
of lean body mass.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.960
Prolonged weightlessness
or bedrest,

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:16.080
regardless of tilt,

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.040
can result
in muscle and bone loss.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.080
But just sleeping on a slant
by putting a few bricks

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.120
under the posts
at the foot of your bed

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:26.480
could potentially give you
a boost in fat metabolism

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:29.080
without
the long-term adverse effects.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.560
If you want to try it,
a note of caution:

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.240
take it slow
when standing back up.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.800
After just four hours
of a six-degree head-down tilt,

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:42.520
most people experience reduced
"orthostatic tolerance."

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.040
When anyone stands suddenly

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.560
after sitting or lying down
for a while,

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:46.680
you can get a "head rush,"

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:48.400
feel dizzy, faint,
or lightheaded

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.920
as the blood drains
from your brain

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.960
down into your legs before
your body can compensate.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.560
This can be exacerbated

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.160
by lying
with your head tilted back,

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.520
so be careful,
get up gradually.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:01.920
Drinking two cups (0.50 L)
of cold water

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:05.000
30 minutes before rising
may also help.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.840
Do not try this at home

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.560
if you have any heart
or lung issues

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.840
or problems with your brain
(like head trauma)

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:15.200
or eyes (even a family history
of glaucoma disqualifies you).

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.440
Ask your physician
if they think it's safe

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.720
for you to sleep
in "mild Trendelenburg."

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:24.920
Friedrich Trendelenburg
was a pioneering surgeon

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.080
that popularized the use

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.200
of what was formerly referred to
as "head-down position"

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.920
for certain abdominal
and pelvic procedures.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:35.720
Angling the operating table
back 15 to 30 degrees

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.600
pulls some abdominal organs
out of the way

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.280
to help declutter
the surgical field,

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:42.920
resulting in
what is now widely known

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.480
as the Trendelenburg position.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:49.040
Steep Trendelenburg,
like 25-, 30-degree tilt,

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:52.080
has been associated with
transient visual problems,

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.120
thought due to the increase
in pressure within the eyeball.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.920
Cautions have been issued
for those at risk for glaucoma

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.560
(a disease
of increased eye pressure)

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:01.600
to avoid "inversion" therapy,

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.000
where people hang upside down,

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.480
as well as yoga positions
like handstands,

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:07.160
which can have a similar effect.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:09.240
Lying back
in mild Trendelenburg,

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:10.480
like around six degrees,

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:13.160
can cause a fleeting bump
in eye pressure

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:15.640
that appears to normalize
within a few hours,

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.080
but the pooling of blood
in the head

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:19.080
may reduce blood flow
to the retina

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.880
sufficient
to impair nerve impulses.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:24.360
Similar effects have been noted
within the brain.

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.120
Intracranial pressure
also normalizes

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:30.200
after a few hours
at a six-degree head-down tilt,

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:31.960
but the overall blood flow
through the brain

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.440
does drop a bit.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:34.800
This is why
you shouldn't try this

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.920
if you have eye
or brain pathology.

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:37.840
To my surprise,

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:41.520
sleeping in mild Trendelenburg
was actually put to the test

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.080
to prevent bone loss
in sedentary individuals.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.440
Restrict people's activity

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.600
to walking less than two miles
(3.20 km) a day on average,

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:51.440
and within a year
they can lose as much

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:54.560
as 15 percent
of their bone mineral density.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.360
What happened
to those randomized

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.400
to the same exercise restriction

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.800
but also combined with sleeping

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.520
at a two-degree head-down tilt

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.600
that was increased
by two degrees

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.480
about every two months

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.360
so they ended up sleeping
at a 14-degree slant

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.800
(or whatever angle
they felt comfortable with)

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.160
by the end of the year?

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.920
Not only did it completely block
the bone loss,

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.640
they built more bone.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.600
Despite
the movement restriction,

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.480
they ended up
with about 12 percent greater

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.560
bone mineral density
than when they started.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.040
Note that
this bone-building effect

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.880
was only apparent
in sedentary individuals.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:32.240
Another group randomized
to the same mild Trendelenburg,

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.080
but assigned to run

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:35.120
an average of five or six miles
(8 or 9.5 km) a day

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:38.800
just maintained
their same skeletal integrity.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.960
The study was repeated,

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:42.920
and the same remarkable effects
were found.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:46.680
There is something about the
"periodic fluid redistribution"

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.760
that comes with sleeping
tilted back at night

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:51.840
that actively builds
both bone density and volume

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:54.720
after the day-long
stagnant pooling of blood

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.560
in the legs
of sedentary individuals.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:58.800
The research team claims

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.360
that this is just the beginning
to the benefits,

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:04.160
citing "unpublished studies"

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.480
asserting a near panacea
of perks

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:07.880
to sleeping in Trendelenburg.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:11.760
I can't be too critical
of this apparent dodge

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:13.480
when I can't point
to a single study

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.760
supporting my supposition that
it will help with weight loss.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:17.560
As far as I can tell,

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:20.280
it's never been tried
or even proposed.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.520
What I can promise
is that any researchers

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:25.680
who take on the mantle
of putting it to the test

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.640
will definitely have
their study featured

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:31.598
in a video on
NutritionFacts.org.

